# Line endings are part of codefit's contract, not a per-checkout detail.
#
# codefit's SQL/Prisma/TypeScript parsers and its golden JSON baselines compare
# bytes. Without this file, a checkout with core.autocrlf=true materializes every
# fixture with CRLF and the same commit behaves differently than it does on CI:
# statement terminators go uncounted, ALTER TABLE statements stop reducing,
# StructureProven() flips to false, and goldens diff on nothing but the newline.
# Pinning LF makes every checkout byte-identical to the tree CI tests.
#
# The stored blobs are already LF, so this file changes checkout behaviour only —
# it produces no content diff. An existing checkout does NOT pick it up
# retroactively; run `git add --renormalize .` (or take a fresh clone) once.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fixtures whose exact bytes a parser or a golden depends on. Redundant with the
# rule above on purpose: it names what breaks if that rule is ever narrowed.
*.sql    text eol=lf
*.prisma text eol=lf
*.ts     text eol=lf
*.tsx    text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf

# Binary: never rewrite these bytes.
*.webp binary
